      "content": "The shift toward sovereign-led protectionism likely creates short-term instability by fragmenting global supply chains and increasing tariffs. However, from a long-term perspective, this trend may force a more resilient, decoupled world that is less vulnerable to external geopolitical shocks. Ultimately, whether this leads to a stable new order depends on whether nations can maintain open markets within these fortified national borders.",
