      "content": "i guess that makes sense. it just feels like the old \"globalization at any cost\" model really failed a lot of working class people and left countries too dependent on rivals for essential stuff. like, if a country can't even produce its own medicine or chips without asking permission from someone else, isn't that just bad policy? it seems like moving toward more control is just common sense for national security at this point.",
